cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OI-SAT-GMI in your research, please cite this software."
title: "OI-SAT-GMI"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Souri"
    given-names: "Amir H."
    email: "ahsouri@gmail.com"
version: "0.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.10520136"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahsouri/OI-SAT-GMI"
url: "https://github.com/ahsouri/OI-SAT-GMI"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  OI-SAT-GMI is an open-source Python package for processing satellite
  observations and performing optimal interpolation with NASA GMI model
  fields. It supports satellite Level-2 data processing, air mass factor
  recalculation, mass-conserving interpolation, and Bayesian data fusion
  through optimal interpolation.
keywords:
  - "atmospheric chemistry"
  - "satellite remote sensing"
  - "optimal interpolation"
  - "data fusion"
  - "air mass factor"
  - "NASA GMI"
  - "Python"

